-- CAPABILITY --------- errors/cap_grant_exceeded_2.march

`main` is granted `Cap(IO.Console)`, but the program reaches `IO.FileRead` (reached from `main`: main → slurp → File.read). The grant is a ceiling on the WHOLE program — declaring `needs IO.FileRead` does not raise it. [cap_grant_exceeded]
help: add a `Cap(IO.FileRead)` parameter to `main` (e.g. `fn main(…, _cap_fileread : Cap(IO.FileRead))`), or widen the whole grant to `Cap(IO)`, or remove the use.

33 |   fn main(cap : Cap(IO.Console)) : () do
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^




fix [cap_grant_exceeded]:
